ansportation and Public Works","ranked":true,"stage":"passed_one_chamber","summary":"Spending Aviation Fees for Equipment, Guaranteeing Upgraded and Advanced Risk Detection and Safety Act of 2026 or the SAFEGUARDS Act of 2026 This bill allocates additional funding for the Transportation Security Administration (TSA) for aviation security, including checked baggage explosives detection equipment and security checkpoint technology. As background, TSA collects passenger civil...","summarySource":"crs","title":"SAFEGUARDS Act of 2026","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/8770"},{"bipartisan":true,"cosponsors":2,"crossPartyCosponsors":1,"id":"hr5447-119","introducedDate":"2025-09-17","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-09-17","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Science, Space, and Technology."},"number":"HR 5447","policyArea":"Science, Technology, Communications","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Amends federal space transportation law to expand the definition of eligible grant recipients, allow the Secretary of Transportation to waive the 90 percent cost-share limitation when in the national interest, and authorize $10 million annually for modernization grants while requiring reports on space transportation demand and funding options.","summarySource":"ai","title":"SPACEPORT Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5447"},{"bipartisan":true,"cosponsors":6,"crossPartyCosponsors":2,"id":"hres560-119","introducedDate":"2025-06-27","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-06-27","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Science, Space, and Technology."},"number":"HRES 560","policyArea":"Science, Technology, Communications","ranked":false,"stage":"introduced","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"title":"Commemorating the 65th anniversary of the Marshall Space Flight Center and recognizing its continued leadership in the development of the Space Launch System and human space exploration.","type":"hres","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-resolution/560"},{"bipartisan":true,"cosponsors":24,"crossPartyCosponsors":12,"id":"hr3312-119","introducedDate":"2025-05-08","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-05-08","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"number":"HR 3312","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Authorizes the Attorney General to make grants to states, local governments, and Indian Tribal governments to create and operate veterans response teams within law enforcement agencies. The five-year pilot program supports teams that provide specialized training, coordinate crisis response, and connect veteran officers and community members with veterans' services.","summarySource":"ai","title":"SERVICE Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/3312"},{"bipartisan":true,"cosponsors":17,"crossPartyCosponsors":3,"id":"hr1438-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-18","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-02-18","text":"Referred to the Committee on Agriculture, and in addition to the Committees on Foreign Affairs, and Intelligence (Permanent Select), for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned."},"number":"HR 1438","policyArea":"Agriculture and Food","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Protecting America's Agricultural Land from Foreign Harm Act of 2025 This bill prohibits persons associated with the governments of Iran, North Korea, China, or Russia from purchasing or leasing agricultural land in the United States. Specifically, the President must prohibit any person (individual or entity) owned by, controlled by, or subject to the jurisdiction or direction of these foreign...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Protecting America’s Agricultural Land from Foreign Harm Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/1438"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":19,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr1351-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-02-13","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Education and Workforce."},"number":"HR 1351","policyArea":"Education","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Promoting American Patriotism In Our Schools Act This bill requires local educational agencies (LEAs) to establish, maintain, and enforce policies that require federally funded public elementary and secondary schools to display the U.S. flag, educate students about the U.S. flag, and direct students and staff to recite the Pledge of Allegiance on a daily basis. Specifically, LEAs, as a condition...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Promoting American Patriotism In Our Schools Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/1351"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":2,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr1146-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-07","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-02-07","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Energy and Commerce."},"number":"HR 1146","policyArea":"Science, Technology, Communications","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"No More Funding for NPR Act of 2025 This bill prohibits federal funding of National Public Radio (NPR) or any successor organization and rescinds certain funds that were provided to NPR. The prohibition includes the payment of dues to or the purchase of programming from NPR by a public broadcast station using federal funds. The prohibition does not include funds made available to NPR during...","summarySource":"crs","title":"No More Funding for NPR Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/1146"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":2,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr901-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-31","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-03-11","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Homeland Security and Governmental Affairs."},"number":"HR 901","policyArea":"Science, Technology, Communications","ranked":true,"stage":"passed_one_chamber","summary":"Research Security and Accountability in DHS Act This bill requires the Science and Technology Directorate in the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) to develop a department-wide policy for safeguarding research and development from unauthorized access or disclosures of sensitive information in related acquisitions. Additionally, the Government Accountability Office must report on the compliance...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Research Security and Accountability in DHS Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/901"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":1,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr706-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-23","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-03-12","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Homeland Security and Governmental Affairs."},"number":"HR 706","policyArea":"Government Operations and Politics","ranked":true,"stage":"passed_one_chamber","summary":"DHS Biodetection Improvement Act This bill directs the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) to assess how it has utilized Department of Energy national laboratories and sites for research and development in carrying out DHS missions and to report to Congress a strategy for how DHS will conduct biodetection research and development in coordination with such laboratories and sites.","summarySource":"crs","title":"DHS Biodetection Improvement Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/706"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr707-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-23","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-23","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"number":"HR 707","policyArea":"Immigration","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Deport Illegal Voters Act of 2025 This bill increases immigration restrictions for non-U.S. nationals ( aliens under federal law) who vote in violation of a federal, state, or local constitutional provision, statute, ordinance, or regulation. Specifically, the bill adds such an act to the list of aggravated felonies that are grounds for deportation and inadmissibility. Under current law, this act...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Deport Illegal Voters Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/707"},{"bipartisan":true,"cosponsors":8,"crossPartyCosponsors":1,"id":"hr708-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-23","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-03-11","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Homeland Security and Governmental Affairs."},"number":"HR 708","policyArea":"Immigration","ranked":true,"stage":"passed_one_chamber","summary":"Strategic Homeland Intelligence and Enforcement Legislation to Defend Against the CCP Act or the SHIELD Against CCP Act This bill requires the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) to form a working group tasked with duties related to countering terrorist, cybersecurity, border and port security, and transportation security threats posed to the United States by the Chinese Communist Party (CCP)....","summarySource":"crs","title":"SHIELD Against CCP Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/708"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr709-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-23","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-24","text":"Referred to the Subcommittee on Aviation."},"number":"HR 709","policyArea":"Transportation and Public Works","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"National Training Center for Counter-Unmanned Aircraft Systems Act This bill requires the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and the Department of Justice (DOJ) to establish training and qualification standards for counter-unmanned aircraft systems, commonly referred to as counter-drone systems. Specifically, DHS and DOJ, in coordination with the Federal Aviation Administration, must establish...","summarySource":"crs","title":"National Training Center for Counter-Unmanned Aircraft Systems Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/709"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":3,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hres37-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-13","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Armed Services."},"number":"HRES 37","policyArea":"Armed Forces and National Security","ranked":false,"stage":"introduced","summary":"This resolution expresses recognition that the Air Force’s Strategic Basing Action process complied with law and policy and was justified in identifying Huntsville, Alabama, as the preferred permanent location for Space Command Headquarters.","summarySource":"crs","title":"Recognizing the 4th anniversary of the Trump administration's Secretary of the Air Force announcing Redstone Arsenal in Huntsville, Alabama, as the preferred location for United States Space Command Headquarters.","type":"hres","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-resolution/37"}],"state":"AL","topCrossPartyCollaborators":[{"bioguideId":"F000481","caucus":"D","count":4,"name":"Shomari Figures"},{"bioguideId":"G000604","caucus":"D","count":2,"name":"Maggie Goodlander"},{"bioguideId":"V000138","caucus":"D","count":2,"name":"Eugene Simon Vindman"},{"bioguideId":"A000148","caucus":"D","count":2,"name":"Jake Auchincloss"},{"bioguideId":"K000402","caucus":"D","count":2,"name":"Timothy M. Kennedy"}]}
